{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/REST Resource Representation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/REST Resource Representation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"rest resource representation rest resource representation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/REST Resource Representation.md","fileName":"REST Resource Representation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"REST Resource Representation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 10:58\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[REST Architectural Constraints and Hypermedia]]","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/REST Resource Representation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/REST Resource Representation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"rest resource representation rest resource representation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/REST Resource Representation.md","fileName":"REST Resource Representation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"REST Resource Representation","heading":"REST Resource Representation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A REST resource is the conceptual target identified by a URI, while a representation is the transferred description of its current or proposed state. JSON, XML, or another media type can represent the same resource without being the resource itself.\n\nClients manipulate a resource by sending and receiving representations through HTTP methods. Separating identity from representation lets the server change internal storage while preserving the public address and agreed message semantics.","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/REST Resource Representation.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/REST Resource Representation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"rest resource representation rest resource representation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/REST Resource Representation.md","fileName":"REST Resource Representation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"REST Resource Representation","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf]]","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}